==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Via {{etyl|la}} {{term|apsis|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc}} {{term|ἁψίς||arch, vault|sc=Polytonic|tr=hapsis|lang=grc}}. See also {{term|apse}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|aps|ides}}

# {{architecture}} A [[recess]] or [[projection]], with a [[dome]] or [[vault]], at the [[east]] end of a [[church]]; an [[apse]].
# {{astronomy}} Either of the [[point]]s in the [[elliptical]] [[orbit]] of a [[planet]] or [[comet]] where it is [[closest]] or [[furthest]] from the [[sun]]; [[perihelion]] or [[aphelion]]; an [[apside]]

